IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `crm-time`

-- Crimes Act 1914 (Commonwealth) -- sections 4AA and 4AB: penalty units,
-- their indexation, and the conversion of a penalty stated in dollars.
--
-- Where a rule answers MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE where the text gives the
-- result, JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING where
-- the text does not speak. Where a rule answers a number, the arithmetic is
-- in crm-time.l4 and the rule that decides whether the provision applies is
-- the MAYBE BOOLEAN one beside it.
--
-- The Consumer Price Index numbers of s 4AA(4) are published by the
-- Australian Statistician and are not among the sources, so they are inputs.
-- The Minister's publication under s 4AA(1A) is an input to the seat layer.

§ `Crimes Act 1914 (Cth) ss 4AA-4AB: penalty units`

§§ `Section 4AA(1) to (2): the penalty unit, and Territory Ordinance`

-- src:4337 | (1) In a law of the Commonwealth or a Territory Ordinance, unless the contrary intention appears:
-- src:4338 | penalty unit means the amount of $330 (subject to indexation under subsection (3)).
@ref s 4AA(1) (src:4337-4338)
GIVEN `the law is a law of the Commonwealth or a Territory Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AA(1) a penalty unit means the amount mentioned in that subsection` IS
    IF NOT `the law is a law of the Commonwealth or a Territory Ordinance`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4339 | (1A) If the amount of a penalty unit is indexed under subsection (3), the Minister must, by notifiable instrument, publish the amount of a penalty unit. However, a failure by the Minister to do so does not invalidate the indexation.
@ref s 4AA(1A) (src:4339)
GIVEN `the amount of a penalty unit has been indexed under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AA(1A) the Minister must, by notifiable instrument, publish the amount of a penalty unit` IS
    IF `the amount of a penalty unit has been indexed under subsection (3)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4339 | (1A) If the amount of a penalty unit is indexed under subsection (3), the Minister must, by notifiable instrument, publish the amount of a penalty unit. However, a failure by the Minister to do so does not invalidate the indexation.
@ref s 4AA(1A) (src:4339)
GIVEN `the Minister has published the amount of a penalty unit by notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AA(1A) a failure by the Minister to publish the amount invalidates the indexation` IS
    IF `the Minister has published the amount of a penalty unit by notifiable instrument`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "Territory Ordinance means an ordinance that (a) ... and (b) ...; and
-- includes a regulation made under such an ordinance."
-- src:4340 | (2) In this section:
-- src:4341 | Territory Ordinance means an ordinance that:
-- src:4342 | (a) was made under an Act providing for the acceptance, administration or government of a Territory; and
-- src:4343 | (b) has not become an enactment of the Australian Capital Territory;
-- src:4344 | and includes a regulation made under such an ordinance.
@ref s 4AA(2) (src:4340-4344)
GIVEN `it is an ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made under an Act providing for the acceptance, administration or government of a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has become an enactment of the Australian Capital Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a regulation made under such an ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AA(2) a Territory Ordinance` IS
    BRANCH IF `it is a regulation made under such an ordinance` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `it is an ordinance` THEN JUST (`it was made under an Act providing for the acceptance, administration or government of a Territory` AND (NOT `it has become an enactment of the Australian Capital Territory`))
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:4338 | penalty unit means the amount of $330 (subject to indexation under subsection (3)).
@ref s 4AA(1) (src:4338)
GIVEN `the number of penalty units` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of one penalty unit, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4AA(1) the number of dollars in a penalty of a number of penalty units` IS
    `the number of penalty units` TIMES `the amount of one penalty unit, in dollars`

§§ `Section 4AA(3) to (7): indexation of the penalty unit`

-- The sidecar formula for s 4AA(3) is
--   Indexation factor for the indexation day x Dollar amount immediately before the indexation day
-- src:4346 | (3) On 1 July 2026 and each third 1 July following that day (an indexation day), the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is replaced by the amount worked out using the following formula:
@ref s 4AA(3) (src:4346)
GIVEN `the indexation day` IS A DATE
      `the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) immediately before the indexation day` IS A NUMBER
      `the index number for the reference quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the index number for the base quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4AA(3) the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) after the indexation day` IS
    IF NOT (`a day is an indexation day` `the indexation day`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the indexation factor for an indexation day` `the index number for the reference quarter` `the index number for the base quarter`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (`the dollar amount after an indexation, to the nearest whole dollar` f `the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) immediately before the indexation day`)

-- The sidecar formula for s 4AA(4) is
--   Index number for the reference quarter / Index number for the base quarter
-- src:4347 | (4) The indexation factor for an indexation day is the number worked out using the following formula:
-- src:4348 | where:
@ref s 4AA(4) (src:4347-4348)
GIVEN `the index number for the reference quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the index number for the base quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4AA(4) the indexation factor for an indexation day` IS
    `the indexation factor for an indexation day` `the index number for the reference quarter` `the index number for the base quarter`

-- src:4349 | base quarter means the March quarter 3 years before the reference quarter.
@ref s 4AA(4) base quarter (src:4349)
GIVEN `the first day of the quarter` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the quarter` IS A DATE
      `the indexation day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AA(4) a quarter is the base quarter for the indexation day` IF
        `the last day of the quarter` EQUALS `the day on which the base quarter ends` `the indexation day`
    AND `the first day of the quarter ending on` `the last day of the quarter` EQUALS JUST `the first day of the quarter`

-- src:4350 | index number, for a quarter, means the All Groups Consumer Price Index number (being the weighted average of the 8 capital cities) published by the Australian Statistician for that quarter.
@ref s 4AA(4) index number (src:4350)
GIVEN `it is the All Groups Consumer Price Index number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the weighted average of the 8 capital cities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was published by the Australian Statistician for that quarter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AA(4) a number is the index number for a quarter` IF
        `it is the All Groups Consumer Price Index number`
    AND `it is the weighted average of the 8 capital cities`
    AND `it was published by the Australian Statistician for that quarter`

-- src:4351 | March quarter means a quarter ending on 31 March.
@ref s 4AA(4) March quarter (src:4351)
GIVEN `the first day of the quarter` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the quarter` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AA(4) a period is a March quarter` IF
        `a March quarter ends on` `the last day of the quarter`
    AND `the first day of the quarter ending on` `the last day of the quarter` EQUALS JUST `the first day of the quarter`

-- src:4352 | reference quarter means the March quarter immediately before the indexation day.
@ref s 4AA(4) reference quarter (src:4352)
GIVEN `the first day of the quarter` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the quarter` IS A DATE
      `the indexation day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AA(4) a quarter is the reference quarter for the indexation day` IF
        `the last day of the quarter` EQUALS `the day on which the reference quarter ends` `the indexation day`
    AND `the first day of the quarter ending on` `the last day of the quarter` EQUALS JUST `the first day of the quarter`

-- src:4353 | (5) An indexation factor is to be calculated to 3 decimal places (rounding up if the fourth decimal place is 5 or more).
@ref s 4AA(5) (src:4353)
GIVEN `the ratio` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4AA(5) an indexation factor calculated to 3 decimal places` IS
    `an indexation factor calculated to 3 decimal places` `the ratio`

-- src:4354 | (6) Amounts worked out under subsection (3) are to be rounded to the nearest whole dollar (rounding 50 cents upwards).
@ref s 4AA(6) (src:4354)
GIVEN `the indexation factor` IS A NUMBER
      `the dollar amount immediately before the indexation day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4AA(6) the amount worked out under subsection (3), rounded to the nearest whole dollar` IS
    `the dollar amount after an indexation, to the nearest whole dollar` `the indexation factor` `the dollar amount immediately before the indexation day`

-- (7)(a) and (b): which published index numbers a calculation uses.
-- src:4355 | (7) Calculations under subsection (4):
-- src:4356 | (a) are to be made using only the index numbers published in terms of the most recently published index reference period; and
-- src:4357 | (b) are to be made disregarding index numbers that are published in substitution for previously published index numbers (except where the substituted numbers are published to take account of changes in the index reference period).
@ref s 4AA(7) (src:4355-4357)
GIVEN `it is published in terms of the most recently published index reference period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published in substitution for a previously published index number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published to take account of a change in the index reference period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AA(7) an index number is used in a calculation under subsection (4)` IS
    IF NOT `it is published in terms of the most recently published index reference period`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it is published in substitution for a previously published index number` AND NOT `it is published to take account of a change in the index reference period`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 4AA(8): which amount applies to an offence`

-- src:4359 | (8) If the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is increased in accordance with subsection (3), the increased amount only applies to offences committed on or after the indexation day.
@ref s 4AA(8) (src:4359)
GIVEN `the dollar amount before the indexation day` IS A NUMBER
      `the dollar amount after the indexation day` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
      `the indexation day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AA(8) the increased amount applies to an offence` IS
    IF (NOT (`a day is an indexation day` `the indexation day`)) OR (NOT (`the dollar amount after the indexation day` GREATER THAN `the dollar amount before the indexation day`))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `an offence was committed on or after the indexation day` `the day of the offence` `the indexation day`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The amount of a penalty unit for an offence. An offence on or after the
-- indexation day gets the replaced amount (s 4AA(3)). Before it, an amount
-- that was increased does not apply (s 4AA(8)), so the amount before does;
-- where the amount was not increased the text does not say which amount
-- applies to an offence before the indexation day, so that is NOTHING.
-- src:4359 | (8) If the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is increased in accordance with subsection (3), the increased amount only applies to offences committed on or after the indexation day.
@ref s 4AA(3), (8) (src:4359)
GIVEN `the dollar amount before the indexation day` IS A NUMBER
      `the dollar amount after the indexation day` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
      `the indexation day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4AA(3), (8) the amount of a penalty unit for an offence` IS
    IF NOT (`a day is an indexation day` `the indexation day`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `an offence was committed on or after the indexation day` `the day of the offence` `the indexation day`
         THEN JUST `the dollar amount after the indexation day`
         ELSE IF `the dollar amount after the indexation day` GREATER THAN `the dollar amount before the indexation day`
              THEN JUST `the dollar amount before the indexation day`
              ELSE IF `the dollar amount after the indexation day` EQUALS `the dollar amount before the indexation day`
                   THEN JUST `the dollar amount before the indexation day`
                   ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 4AB: conversion of pecuniary penalties expressed in dollar amounts`

-- src:4361 | (1) A reference in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory Ordinance to a pecuniary penalty of D dollars, where D is a number, is taken to be a reference to a pecuniary penalty of P penalty units, where P is:
@ref s 4AB(1) (src:4361)
GIVEN `the reference is in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AB(1) a reference to a pecuniary penalty of D dollars is taken to be a reference to a pecuniary penalty of P penalty units` IS
    IF `the reference is in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory Ordinance` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4361 | (1) A reference in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory Ordinance to a pecuniary penalty of D dollars, where D is a number, is taken to be a reference to a pecuniary penalty of P penalty units, where P is:
-- src:4362 | (a) if D ÷ 100 is a whole number—that whole number; or
-- src:4363 | (b) if D ÷ 100 is not a whole number—the next highest whole number.
@ref s 4AB(1) (src:4361-4363)
GIVEN `D` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4AB(1) P is` IS
    `the number of penalty units that a penalty of D dollars is taken to be` `D`

-- src:4364 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a reference to the maximum amount of a penalty that is not imposed by a court, or by a service tribunal under the Defence Force Discipline Act 1982.
@ref s 4AB(2) (src:4364)
GIVEN `the reference is to the maximum amount of a penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalty is imposed by a court, or by a service tribunal under the Defence Force Discipline Act 1982` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AB(2) subsection (1) applies` IS
    IF `the reference is to the maximum amount of a penalty` AND NOT `the penalty is imposed by a court, or by a service tribunal under the Defence Force Discipline Act 1982`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4365 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to:
-- src:4366 | (a) section 76 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; or
-- src:4367 | (c) a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed for the purposes of this subsection.
@ref s 4AB(3) (src:4365-4367)
GIVEN `the provision is section 76 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed for the purposes of subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AB(3) subsection (1) applies` IS
    IF `the provision is section 76 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010` OR `the provision is a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed for the purposes of subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsections (1), (2) and (3) together. A "does not apply" in (2) or (3)
-- is the text's own no; where none of them speaks, the conversion applies
-- when the reference is in a law of the Commonwealth or a Territory Ordinance.
-- src:4361 | (1) A reference in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory Ordinance to a pecuniary penalty of D dollars, where D is a number, is taken to be a reference to a pecuniary penalty of P penalty units, where P is:
-- src:4362 | (a) if D ÷ 100 is a whole number—that whole number; or
-- src:4363 | (b) if D ÷ 100 is not a whole number—the next highest whole number.
-- src:4364 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a reference to the maximum amount of a penalty that is not imposed by a court, or by a service tribunal under the Defence Force Discipline Act 1982.
-- src:4365 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to:
-- src:4366 | (a) section 76 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; or
-- src:4367 | (c) a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed for the purposes of this subsection.
@ref s 4AB(1), (2), (3) (src:4361-4367)
GIVEN `the reference is in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is to the maximum amount of a penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalty is imposed by a court, or by a service tribunal under the Defence Force Discipline Act 1982` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is section 76 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed for the purposes of subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AB the conversion of a penalty of D dollars to penalty units applies` IS
    BRANCH IF `s 4AB(2) subsection (1) applies` `the reference is to the maximum amount of a penalty` `the penalty is imposed by a court, or by a service tribunal under the Defence Force Discipline Act 1982` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `s 4AB(3) subsection (1) applies` `the provision is section 76 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010` `the provision is a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed for the purposes of subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE `s 4AB(1) a reference to a pecuniary penalty of D dollars is taken to be a reference to a pecuniary penalty of P penalty units` `the reference is in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory Ordinance`

-- src:4368 | (4) In this section:
-- src:4369 | penalty includes a fine.
@ref s 4AB(4) (src:4368-4369)
GIVEN `it is a fine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AB(4) a penalty includes` IS
    IF `it is a fine` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4368 | (4) In this section:
-- src:4369 | penalty includes a fine.
-- src:4370 | Territory Ordinance has the same meaning as in section 4AA.
@ref s 4AB(4) (src:4368-4370)
GIVEN `it is an ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made under an Act providing for the acceptance, administration or government of a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has become an enactment of the Australian Capital Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a regulation made under such an ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4AB(4) Territory Ordinance has the same meaning as in section 4AA` IS
    `s 4AA(2) a Territory Ordinance` `it is an ordinance` `it was made under an Act providing for the acceptance, administration or government of a Territory` `it has become an enactment of the Australian Capital Territory` `it is a regulation made under such an ordinance`
